--key prints one value per file and --keys projects a subset into the normal
per-file block. They describe different output, so asking for both is a mistake
and must be refused rather than silently resolved to one of them. 64 is the
usage exit status.

stderr is not pinned. The refusal is a ValidationError, so ArgumentParser prints
md's sentence followed by the whole usage line for `list`, and that usage line
lists every option the subcommand has. Pinning it would turn "someone added a
flag to list" into a failure of this case, which guards something else entirely.
